import lib/process.dl
import lib/text.dl

to get the test interpreter for termination handlers:
    return "python" if the process platform is Windows, else "python3"

class:
    patterns:
        [a|] reading state
    members:
        success as a boolean
        completion as a boolean
        stream ending as a boolean

{reading state:state} succeeded means: state's success

{reading state:state} is complete means: state's completion

{reading state:state} is incomplete means: not state's completion

{reading state:state} awaits the stream ending means: not state's stream ending

{reading state:state} should continue means: (state succeeded) and ((state is incomplete) and (state awaits the stream ending))

set command to a process command for the test interpreter for termination handlers
add "-u" as an argument to command
add "-c" as an argument to command
add "import os,signal,sys,time\nif os.name != 'nt': signal.signal(signal.SIGTERM, lambda *_: sys.exit(0))\nsys.stdout.buffer.write(b'ready\\n'); sys.stdout.buffer.flush()\ntime.sleep(30)" as an argument to command
launch command and set child to it

set contents to the string form of ""
set reading to @intrinsic("construct", a reading state, true, false, false)
loop while reading should continue:
    read the standard output of child and set chunk to it
    set reading's success to chunk succeeded
    if reading succeeded:
        set contents to (contents + chunk's contents)
        set reading's completion to contents ends with "\n"
        set reading's stream ending to chunk reached the end of stream
terminate child and set termination to it
wait for child and set status to it
set expected to 0 as a 64 bit integer
if the process platform is Windows:
    set expected to 1 as a 64 bit integer

print lines (child was launched), ((reading succeeded) and (reading is complete)) and (contents = "ready\n")
print lines (termination succeeded), (status succeeded), (status reports completion) and (status reports termination)
print lines (status's exit code = expected) and (status's termination signal = (0 as a 32 bit integer))
